en more richly  valued despite having far inferior  growth prospects also the recent  sell-off hasn't made their valuation  that much better nvidia still has a pe  ratio of nearly 50 and a market cap of  460 billion dollars and thus far nvidia  has only been reporting stellar quarters  imagine if nvidia has just one quarter  of stagnation or even a decline their  current valuation would just become even  less justified causing investors to sell  off the stock even further and don't  think that just because nvidia has  already dropped 50 means that they can't  drop much further because they  definitely can if mining demand doesn't  recover and the overall market continues  to sell off nvidia can easily crash 80  to 90 percent like it did during the dot  com bust and the 2000 financial  recession really you don't even have to  look that far to realize how much nvidia  can drop just take a look at netflix or  paypal right now  at the end of the day nvidia has been  popped up by several factors for several  years now  first you have the 2017 bitcoin board on  it then there was a 2021 bitcoin forward  on it and now you have a supply shortage  all of these factors have given nvidia  an unprecedented amount of pricing power  and leverage which nvidia has cleverly  used to maximize profits  but as these temporary boosts start to  fade away the short-term future of  nvidia is becoming more and more  uncertain combine this with the fact  that nvidia already had one of the rigid  valuations on the market and it becomes  clear that nvidia's 50 sell-off could it  just be the beginning of something much  more painful  this isn't to say that nvidia is screwed  in the long term by any means though  nvidia produces the best gpus in the  world and they diversified it into  several sectors from machine learning to  artificial intelligence so nvidia is by  no means going anywhere but it's very  likely that we start to see declines in  nvidia's financials as the gpu market  finally cools down and miners move away  from gaming gpus  but if we look past that i think it's  just a matter of time until their  dominant position and massive  investments pay off and nvidia reaches a  trillion dollar valuation but that's  just what i think do you guys have an  nvidia gpu comment that down below also  drop a like if you can't wait for gpu  prices to finally cool down and of  course consider checking out our  international channels to watch your  videos in other languages and consider  subscribing to see more questions  logically answered but until then i'm  hari and i'll see you guys on the next  one

